  "post": {
    "caption": "Queen Mary's dollhouse holds tiny Crown Jewels. Architect Edwin Lutyens designed it as a gift for Queen Mary, with everything built at one inch to the foot. Its strong room holds a full set of miniature Crown Jewels, with tiny crowns set with real gems and seed pearls. The miniature sceptre is only 8 centimeters long. Cartier made seven working clocks for the house, and a tiny Faberge mouse was added. George Bernard Shaw turned down the request to write a tiny book for it. It has been kept at Windsor Castle since 1925.",
